1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Nxe5 d6 4. Nf3 Nxe4 5. d4 d5 6. Bd3 Bd6 7. O-O Bg4 8. c4 O-O 9. h3 Bh5 10. cxd5 f5 11. Nc3 Bxf3 12. Qxf3 Nxc3 13. bxc3 Qd7 14. c4 b6 15. Bb2 Na6 16. c5 Nb4 17. cxd6 Nxd3 18. Qxd3 Qxd6 19. Ba3 Qxd5 20. Bxf8 Rxf8 21. Qb3 Qxb3 22. axb3 a5 23. Rac1 Rf7 24. Rc6 b5 25. Rfc1 h6 26. Rxc7 Rxc7 27. Rxc7 {Source: Chandler scoresheet. Note, the original scoresheet for this game is dated 2 October 1976, and each subsequent scoresheet shows each round being played on succeeding days up to 8 October 1976. However, all other evidence points to the tournament running from 3 to 9 October 1976, including the meticulously-maintained Guernsey Congress website, the report in BCM (January 1977, p16) and Dr JM Aitken's games. All Guernsey tournaments from 1975 for at least ten years started on a Sunday, so this must have been played on 3 October 1976 despite what appears on Murray's scoresheets. JS} 1-0

